{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/micromatch/braces/pulls/78","id":4754168006,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAYS4588AAAABG17Yxg","html_url":"https://github.com/micromatch/braces/pull/78","diff_url":"https://github.com/micromatch/braces/pull/78.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/micromatch/braces/pull/78.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/micromatch/braces/issues/78","number":78,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"fix: bound parser nesting and recursive AST traversal","user":{"login":"thaibaole89","id":283337045,"node_id":"U_kgDOEONhVQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/283337045?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/thaibaole89","html_url":"https://github.com/thaibaole89","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thaibaole89/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thaibaole89/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thaibaole89/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thaibaole89/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thaibaole89/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thaibaole89/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thaibaole89/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thaibaole89/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thaibaole89/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Deeply nested patterns below the existing character limit can overflow the recursive AST walkers. This change rejects excessive nesting with a controlled SyntaxError before the engine exhausts its stack.\r\n\r\n- Cap parser brace/parenthesis nesting and recursive compile/expand/stringify traversal at 100.\r\n- Apply the traversal bound to direct AST `nodes` trees, which bypass parsing.\r\n- Document the bound in README and its .verb source. Parser container nesting and walker call depth have distinct counts at the boundary.\r\n- Preserve ordinary alternatives, ranges, escapes and parsed AST behavior. No version/dependency change.\r\n\r\nAddresses #70 / GHSA-vfj7-8cjw-p6xm. Related to #77, which proposes an opt-in maxDepth option; this proposal provides a mandatory default bound for existing callers that pass no option. Maintainer input on the threshold/API is welcome.\r\n\r\nValidation:\r\n- New regressions against unchanged upstream: 12 fail / 2 pass.\r\n- Builder: `npm test` on Node 24.14.1, 908 pass, including 14 new cases.\r\n- Independent reviewer: full upstream suite on actual Node 8.3.0, 908 pass; new tests 14/14 pass. Removing the shared guard causes 12 failures; individual compile/expand/stringify guards cause 2 failures each, and parser guards 1 failure.\r\n- A 512KB-stack child process checks 4000-level strings; direct AST and 100/101 boundaries are exercised. Ordinary syntax and 99 nested containers retain expected results.\r\n\r\nThis bounds parser and AST `nodes` recursion depth; it does not cap expansion cardinality or claim safety for every malformed AST field/getter/parent structure or resource-exhaustion input. For example, a malformed array-valued text node can still reach unguarded flattening; the parser does not emit that shape. No general CPU/memory or regex-safety claim is made.\r\n\r\nAI assistance: OpenAI Codex was used to prepare the patch, tests and independent review.","created_at":"2026-10-06T04:32:06Z","updated_at":"2026-10-06T04:32:06Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"5beab0bc68dd6b33bf76bc41a942be144c69e76d","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/micromatch/braces/pulls/78/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/micromatch/braces/pulls/78/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/micromatch/braces/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/micromatch/braces/issues/78/c